  'modal.guide.html':`<h2>Your first robotics experiment.</h2><p>A robot’s structure changes how it behaves. This workbench makes that connection visible.</p><ol><li><strong>Build.</strong> Choose a preset or move the sliders to position your payload.</li><li><strong>Predict.</strong> Will your rover stay balanced at the target ramp angle?</li><li><strong>Test.</strong> Run the ramp test. Watch the orange gravity line move relative to the green support polygon.</li><li><strong>Improve.</strong> Change one variable and try again. Compare runs in Results.</li></ol><h3>Ready to make it move?</h3><p>Open <strong>Code</strong> to give the wheels instructions. Choose flat, rough, or slippery ground in the builder. After a run, open <strong>Plots</strong> to read the encoders, the IMU, and the motors.</p><p>Your design, code, and last 30 experiments are saved in this browser on this device.</p>`,
